{"id": "unknown-2026-06-12-002", "date": "2026-06-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["slow", "weak", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "South India cotton yarn continues to see sluggish demand, prices down", "content": "South India’s cotton yarn market remained under pressure as weak demand, labour shortages and slower downstream activity weighed on prices.\nMumbai yarn prices fell by ₹5–7 per kg, while Tiruppur remained stable but sluggish.\nCotton prices in Gujarat were steady, though bearish sentiment, weaker demand and lower CCI prices continued to discourage fresh buying.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/south-india-cotton-yarn-continues-to-see-sluggish-demand-prices-down-310963-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-12-003", "date": "2026-06-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "World cotton supply-demand outlook may tighten next year: WASDE", "content": "USDA’s June WASDE report points to a tighter global cotton balance in 2026–27, with lower beginning and ending stocks and slightly higher consumption.\nWorld production is forecast to remain stable at 116.04 million bales, while demand rises, led by China.\nFor 2025–26, stronger exports are expected to reduce global ending stocks and tighten supply further.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/world-cotton-supply-demand-outlook-may-tighten-next-year-wasde-310956-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-12-004", "date": "2026-06-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["strong demand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Strong export demand boosts US cotton sales and shipments", "content": "US cotton export demand strengthened in the week ended June 4, with Upland sales rising 12 per cent to 207,000 RB and shipments increasing 12 per cent to 300,100 RB.\nVietnam, Pakistan and India led buying.\nNew-crop Upland sales surged to 298,700 RB.\nPima shipments hit a marketing-year high of 22,900 RB, driven by strong demand from India and Pakistan.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/strong-export-demand-boosts-us-cotton-sales-and-shipments-310950-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-12-005", "date": "2026-06-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ICE cotton bounces back on short covering, positive US reports", "content": "ICE cotton futures rebounded on technical short covering, strong US export sales and a supportive USDA WASDE report showing lower global ending stocks.\nJuly futures settled at 72.49 cents/lb and December at 76.39 cents/lb.\nSofter US inflation improved sentiment, but traders remain cautious as volatility is expected ahead of First Notice Day and options expiry.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-bounces-back-on-short-covering-positive-us-reports-310946-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-12-006", "date": "2026-06-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh-Japan EPA opens $3 bn apparel export door with RMG push", "content": "Bangladesh aims to raise apparel exports to Japan from about $1.3-1.4 billion to $3 billion, requiring monthly shipments to roughly double. \nThe 2026 EPA secures duty-free access and flexible rules of origin, boosting competitiveness. \nSuccess will depend on converting buyer interest into repeat orders through stronger quality, compliance, sourcing and Japan-focused execution.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bangladesh-japan-epa-opens-3-bn-apparel-export-door-with-rmg-push-310945-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-12-007", "date": "2026-06-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.33, "keywords": ["growth", "decline", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "US' Oxford Industries' Q1 sales slip 0.4% amid tariffs", "content": "Oxford Industries has reported Q1 net sales of $391 million, broadly flat YoY, while adjusted EPS declined to $1.39 due to $11 million in additional tariff costs. \nTommy Bahama delivered growth, but Lilly Pulitzer and Johnny Was sales weakened. \nThe company narrowed its FY26 sales outlook to $1.475-1.505 billion while maintaining confidence that lower tariffs. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/us-oxford-industries-q1-sales-slip-0-4-amid-tariffs-310943-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-12-008", "date": "2026-06-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.33, "keywords": ["growth", "decline", "slow"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Cambodia garment exports maintain growth despite May slowdown", "content": "Cambodia’s apparel exports rose 5.6 per cent YoY to $4.45 billion in January-May 2026, accounting for 31.7 per cent of total exports.\nGrowth was driven by both knitted and woven garments, although May shipments declined 7.3 per cent.\nCotton and cotton yarn imports surged 27.1 per cent, signalling stronger demand for cotton-based apparel production.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/cambodia-garment-exports-maintain-growth-despite-may-slowdown-310906-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
